# Every step of the demosaic, side by side.
#
# The pipeline is only three things: interpolate the two missing colours at
# each photosite, apply the camera's white balance gains, rotate through the
# camera matrix into sRGB. Panels 2 and 4 exist to show WHY the highlight
# clamp is in there -- compare them against 3 and 5.
#
# Panel 6 is the diagnostic map: what the matrix DID to each pixel.
#   red   = hue shift (0..30 deg)
#   green = saturation gain -- pushed away from grey (0..0.5)
#   blue  = a channel driven negative (0..1)
# Green is the one to watch. The matrix's own rotation is bounded and
# hue-dependent, so red alone does not mark a fault; saturation gain is what
# separates the halo from ordinary colour.
#
# Drop a raw file onto the "test" row.

src = mosaic("test")

interp, balanced, clamped, unclamped, out, shift = demosaic_stages(src)

display(interp,    "1 interpolated (raw scale)")
display(balanced,  "2 white balance, NO clamp")
display(clamped,   "3 white balance WITH clamp")
display(unclamped, "4 matrix without the clamp -- the magenta")
display(out,       "5 final")
display(shift,     "6 what the matrix did (G = saturation gain)")
